{"sections":{"main":{"type":"main-page","blocks":{"heading":{"type":"text","name":"Title","settings":{"text":"<p>So machst du das perfekte Foto!<\/p>","width":"100%","max_width":"normal","alignment":"center","type_preset":"custom","font":"var(--font-heading--family)","font_size":"2rem","line_height":"normal","letter_spacing":"normal","case":"none","wrap":"pretty","color":"var(--color-foreground-heading)","background":false,"background_color":"#00000026","corner_radius":0,"padding-block-start":0,"padding-block-end":0,"padding-inline-start":0,"padding-inline-end":0},"blocks":{}},"text_aePKkr":{"type":"text","name":"t:names.text","settings":{"text":"<p>Damit dein Haustierposter perfekt wird, ist es wichtig, dass du ein gutes Foto machst. Hier sind die wichtigsten Punkte, auf die du achten solltest:<\/p><p><\/p>","width":"100%","max_width":"none","alignment":"center","type_preset":"custom","font":"var(--font-body--family)","font_size":"0.875rem","line_height":"normal","letter_spacing":"normal","case":"none","wrap":"pretty","color":"var(--color-foreground)","background":false,"background_color":"#00000026","corner_radius":0,"padding-block-start":10,"padding-block-end":0,"padding-inline-start":0,"padding-inline-end":0},"blocks":{}},"text_UGwAjc":{"type":"text","name":"t:names.text","settings":{"text":"<p><\/p><p><strong>Fotoqualität<\/strong><\/p><p><em><strong>Licht: <\/strong><\/em>Verwende Tageslicht oder stelle sicher, dass der Raum gut beleuchtet ist.<\/p><p><em><strong>Kamera: <\/strong><\/em>Nutze ein Smartphone mit guter Kamera oder eine Digitalkamera. Achte darauf, dass das Bild scharf ist – keine Screenshots oder Bilder aus WhatsApp.<\/p><p><em><strong>Größe:<\/strong><\/em> Dein Foto sollte mindestens 2 MB groß sein, um eine gute Druckqualität zu gewährleisten.<\/p><p><em><strong>Bearbeitung<\/strong><\/em>: Verzichte auf starke Filter oder Bearbeitungen, um das natürliche Bild deines Haustiers zu erhalten.<\/p>","width":"100%","max_width":"none","alignment":"center","type_preset":"custom","font":"var(--font-body--family)","font_size":"0.875rem","line_height":"normal","letter_spacing":"normal","case":"none","wrap":"pretty","color":"var(--color-foreground)","background":false,"background_color":"#00000026","corner_radius":0,"padding-block-start":30,"padding-block-end":0,"padding-inline-start":0,"padding-inline-end":0},"blocks":{}},"text_GM7TgW":{"type":"text","name":"t:names.text","settings":{"text":"<p><\/p><p><strong>Die richtige Perspektive<\/strong><\/p><p><em><strong>Position<\/strong><\/em>: Fotografiere dein Tier möglichst frontal und auf Augenhöhe. Das Gesicht und der Hals sollten gut sichtbar und scharf sein.<\/p><p><em><strong>Keine Schatten<\/strong><\/em>: Achte darauf, dass das Gesicht deines Tieres ohne Schatten gut zu erkennen ist.<\/p>","width":"100%","max_width":"none","alignment":"center","type_preset":"custom","font":"var(--font-body--family)","font_size":"0.875rem","line_height":"normal","letter_spacing":"normal","case":"none","wrap":"pretty","color":"var(--color-foreground)","background":false,"background_color":"#00000026","corner_radius":0,"padding-block-start":30,"padding-block-end":0,"padding-inline-start":0,"padding-inline-end":0},"blocks":{}},"group_dJfKVa":{"type":"group","name":"t:names.group","settings":{"content_direction":"row","vertical_on_mobile":true,"horizontal_alignment":"flex-start","vertical_alignment":"center","align_baseline":false,"horizontal_alignment_flex_direction_column":"center","vertical_alignment_flex_direction_column":"center","gap":75,"width":"fill","custom_width":100,"width_mobile":"fill","custom_width_mobile":100,"height":"fit","custom_height":100,"inherit_color_scheme":true,"color_scheme":"","background_media":"none","video_position":"cover","background_image_position":"cover","border":"none","border_width":1,"border_opacity":100,"border_radius":0,"toggle_overlay":false,"overlay_color":"#00000026","overlay_style":"solid","gradient_direction":"to top","link":"","open_in_